# PHASE 2 — ASSESSMENT TYPES AND ACCESS CONTROL

## Priority: P0

Implement the following assessment access policy exactly.

| Assessment type | Requires access code | Access policy |
|---|---|---|
| Tests | YES | Access code required |
| Examinations | YES | Access code required |
| Assignments | NO | Can be taken without an access code |
| Activities | NO | Can be taken without an access code |

Rules:

1. Only tests and examinations require assessment access codes.
2. Assignments and activities must never display an unnecessary access-code prompt.
3. Students should be able to access assignments and activities without entering a code.
4. Preserve their existing availability and publication workflow.
5. Do not confuse school registration codes or other portal access codes with assessment access codes.
6. Access-code verification must be properly secured. Never expose confidential assessment codes or answer keys in publicly readable documents.
7. Where an access code is required, enforce validation before the student enters the test or examination.

Do not apply password protection indiscriminately to every assessment type.

