# PHASE 3 — ASSESSMENT AUTO-RELEASE AND AUTOMATIC GRADING

## Priority: P1

This functionality has already been introduced into the portal.

The task is to inspect, preserve, repair and complete it, not to remove it or create a duplicate.

## 3.1 Auto-release configuration

Tutors must be able to configure an assessment for automatic release.

The setting must be visible and functional in the tutor's assessment creation and editing interface.

When enabled:

- The configured release date/time must be saved.
- The tutor must be able to see the automatic-release configuration.
- The saved assessment must correctly reflect its release status.
- The assessment must become available to its intended students at the configured time.
- Release must not depend on the tutor manually opening the portal at that time.
- Students must see the assessment when it becomes available.

Inspect the existing implementation before deciding how to repair its scheduling mechanism.

Do not replace a working auto-release implementation unnecessarily.

## 3.2 Automatic grading

When a tutor enables automatic grading:

- Grade eligible questions automatically after submission.
- Calculate the student's score correctly.
- Preserve the grading result.
- Respect the configured result-release setting.
- Make results available to students immediately when the assessment is released, provided automatic grading has completed.

Students should not unnecessarily wait for tutors to manually publish automatically graded results.

Manual-deliverable assessments must retain their manual review process. Do not automatically award grades for deliverables that require tutor evaluation.

## 3.3 Separate grading and release states

Ensure that grading completion and result publication are not treated as the same operation.

An assessment may be:

- Submitted but not graded.
- Automatically graded but awaiting configured release.
- Manually graded and awaiting tutor release.
- Graded and released.

Preserve the existing data model wherever possible.

