# PHASE 6 — ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT

## Priority: P1

Implement a consistent attendance system across the relevant portals.

Attendance must be recorded by authorised tutors or administrators and displayed according to the user's relationship with the student.

## 6.1 Attendance visibility

| Role | What they can see |
|---|---|
| Super Admin | All students' attendance |
| School Admin | All attendance records belonging to their school |
| School Student | Their own attendance |
| Individual Student | Their own attendance |
| Parent | Attendance records of their enrolled children |
| Tutor | Attendance records for their assigned students/classes |
| Other Sub-admins | Only attendance access specifically granted to their role |

## 6.2 Attendance modification permissions

Only authorised administrators and tutors should be able to modify attendance records.

Students must not be able to change their attendance.

Parents must not be able to change attendance.

School Students must only have read access to their own attendance records.

School Admins must be restricted to their school's records.

Tutors must be restricted to their assigned students or classes.

## 6.3 Attendance records

Allow authorised users to:

- Mark attendance.
- Update attendance status.
- Correct incorrectly recorded attendance.
- View historical attendance.
- Identify who recorded attendance.
- See when attendance was recorded.
- Review attendance corrections.

Preserve an audit trail of previous values and corrections.

Parents and students should see attendance records without being presented with administrative modification controls.

## 6.4 School isolation

A School Admin must never be able to view another school's students' attendance.

A School Student must never see another student's attendance.

Enforce these restrictions in Firestore security rules and the relevant backend operations, not merely by filtering the displayed interface.

